@startuml 02-deployment
!theme plain
title Deployment — v1 ship vs horizontal scale posture

actor Client

node "Edge (scale add-on)" {
  component "Load Balancer\n(L4/L7 — cloud LB / nginx / Traefik)\n*not provisioned in v1 take-home*" as LB
}

node "Application (same Docker image)" {
  component "API replica 1\nGraphQL + health" as API1
  component "API replica N\n(scale out)" as APIN
  component "Refresh worker ×1\n(schedule-driven)" as Worker
}

database "PostgreSQL\n(primary)" as PG

cloud "Open-Meteo" as OM

Client --> LB
LB --> API1
LB --> APIN
API1 --> PG
APIN --> PG
Worker --> PG
Worker --> OM
API1 ..> OM : cold-start only
APIN ..> OM : cold-start only

note bottom of LB
  v1 local/demo: single API container,
  no LB. App stays **stateless** so an LB
  can be added with zero redesign.
end note

note bottom of Worker
  Keep worker count at 1 until scale
  ladder says otherwise (advisory lock
  / queue if multi-worker needed).
end note

@enduml
